>
  <p>
    <strong>Motasoft's Virtual Garage Manager (VGM) has been around for close to two decades</strong> and is trusted
    by over 1,000 UK garages, according to <a href="https://www.motasoft.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Motasoft's own site</a>.
    It covers the essentials — workshop diary, job sheets, invoicing, <a href="/features/mot-reminders">MOT history and reminders</a> via DVSA — at one of the lower
    entry prices in the market.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing structure</h2>
  <p>
    Motasoft's base price ranges from £50 to £120/month, but DVLA and VRM lookups, MOT data refresh, mailshots and
    SMS reminders reportedly run on top as pay-per-use credits — VRM lookups around 9p each, SMS around 6p each.
    GarageCloud's £50/month Starter plan is a flat fee with no per-lookup or per-message credit charges.
  </p>

  <h2>What Motasoft does well</h2>
  <p>
    VGM has a long track record, a low entry price, and a direct integration with GroupTyre for live tyre ordering
    and pricing — a specific, useful feature for any <a href="/mobile-tyre-fitting-software">workshop that fits tyres regularly</a>. Its core feature set is proven across nearly two decades of UK garage use.
  </p>

  <h2>What to weigh up</h2>
  <p>
    A credit-based model can make the real monthly cost harder to predict than a flat fee, particularly for a
    workshop that sends a lot of SMS reminders or does frequent VRM lookups. GarageCloud's pricing is a single
    monthly number regardless of usage.
  </p>

  <h2>Where GarageCloud is different, not necessarily better</h2>
  <p>
    GarageCloud is pre-launch and doesn't have Motasoft's near-20-year track record or its GroupTyre integration
    yet. A workshop that wants a proven, low-cost system with direct tyre wholesaler ordering has good reason to
    look at Motasoft. A workshop that wants predictable, flat monthly pricing without credit top-ups is the one
    GarageCloud is built for — see <a href="/pricing">GarageCloud pricing</a>, or <a href="/garage-hive-alternatives">other alternatives</a>.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
